  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Core collectibles momentum has returned, fueled by renewed demand for Pop! products and fresh launches like KPop Demon Hunters and Pop! Yourself. An improving entertainment slate and international initiatives are providing tailwinds, while product mix and demand strength are lifting profitability. Prior inventory‑glut fears have receded as stock levels and net debt decline, and the gross‑margin profile has reached new highs. Near‑term revenue guidance is flat to modest, but the quality of earnings is improving markedly.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** The turnaround strategy is gaining credibility: aggressive cost discipline and inventory rationalization have delivered record margins and lower leverage, directly addressing past operational risks. Leadership is guiding for significant earnings expansion even on very modest top‑line growth, signalling a deliberate shift from volume‑chasing to value‑focused execution. Consecutive quarters of debt and inventory reduction, coupled with successful product innovation and an international push, show a team reinvesting from a much healthier foundation, a dynamic that the market now rewards.",
